# ${project.name}

The Checkstyle Plugin runs [Checkstyle](https://checkstyle.org/) on your project's sources and resources.
It can fail the build on violations, or add a Checkstyle report to the project site.

This version of the plugin uses Checkstyle ${checkstyleVersion} by default.
It requires Maven 3.9.0 or later and Java ${javaVersion} or later.
You can [use a newer Checkstyle version](./examples/upgrading-checkstyle.html) at runtime.

Quick Start
-----------

Check the code against the default `sun_checks.xml` ruleset and fail on violations:

```shell
mvn checkstyle:check
```

Check against the Google ruleset instead.
The `google_checks.xml` ruleset reports at `warning` severity, so also lower the severity that counts as a violation:

```shell
mvn checkstyle:check -Dcheckstyle.config.location=google_checks.xml -Dcheckstyle.violationSeverity=warning
```

Write an HTML report to `target/reports/checkstyle.html` without failing the build:

```shell
mvn checkstyle:checkstyle
```

To run the check in every build, bind the `check` goal in your POM, as shown on the [usage page](./usage.html).

The plugin ships two predefined rulesets from Checkstyle: [`sun_checks.xml`](https://checkstyle.org/sun_style.html) (the default) and [`google_checks.xml`](https://checkstyle.org/google_style.html).
You can also [use your own ruleset](./examples/custom-checker-config.html) or [write it inline in the POM](./examples/inline-checker-config.html).
Rulesets from older plugin versions are listed on the [Predefined Rulesets](./config/index.html) page.

Goals Overview
--------------

The Checkstyle Plugin has three goals:

- [checkstyle:check](./check-mojo.html) performs Checkstyle analysis and logs violations to the console.
  It fails the build on violations by default, and binds to the `verify` phase.
  It can also re-use the result of an earlier `checkstyle:checkstyle` run.
- [checkstyle:checkstyle](./checkstyle-mojo.html) is a reporting goal that performs Checkstyle analysis and generates a report on violations.
- [checkstyle:checkstyle-aggregate](./checkstyle-aggregate-mojo.html) is a reporting goal that generates one report for all modules of a multi-module build.
  Run it from the root project.

[checkstyle:help](./help-mojo.html) lists the goals and their parameters.

Usage
-----

General instructions on how to use the Checkstyle Plugin are on the [usage page](./usage.html).
The [examples](#Examples) below describe more specific use cases.
If you still have questions, look at the [FAQ](./faq.html) or ask on the [user mailing list](./mailing-lists.html).

Report a defect or request a feature in the [issue tracker](./issue-management.html).
For a bug, include the steps or a small project that reproduces it.
The source code is in the [source repository](./scm.html).

<a id="Major_Version_Upgrade_to_version_3.0.0"></a>

Upgrading From 2.x
------------------

Version 3.0.0 removed the `sourceDirectory` and `testSourceDirectory` parameters.
Use `sourceDirectories` and `testSourceDirectories` instead.

